/-!
# `Ct`: constant-time proofs for the Aeneas translation of the SLH-DSA crate

* `Ct/Leak.lean`     the leakage monad `Leak α = Result (α × Trace)`, events, `cond`, `loop`,
                     erasure, `erase_loop`.
* `Ct/Do.lean`       `do` notation for `Leak` (Aeneas's elaborator with `Leak.bind`/`Leak.cond`).
* `Ct/Model.lean`    the leakage model: the names of the generated text redefined in
                     `namespace slhdsa_leak` as instrumented primitives (trusted table).
* `Ct/ModelBuild.lean` the build's own part of the model (default build: nothing; `hw-sha2`
                     build: the intrinsic wrappers).
* `Ct/Funs.lean`     GENERATED by `scripts/ct-gen.sh` from `Slhdsa/Funs.lean` (header only).
* `Ct/Check.lean`    checker: constants of the instrumented definitions ⊆ model ∪ whitelist.
* `Ct/CheckTest.lean` name-resolution checks and positive controls for the checker.
* `Ct/Erase.lean`    `slhdsa_leak.f.erase_eq` for every definition of `Slhdsa/Funs.lean` (190).
* `Ct/Rel.lean`      the relational judgment `Rel` (and `RelIf` for public outputs) and rules.
* `Ct/Tactic.lean`   `ct_step`/`ct_steps` lockstep tactic.
* `Ct/Sha256Core.lean` constant-time lemmas for `sha256.rs`: schedule, portable compression.
* `Ct/CompressTop.lean` `sha256::compress` (BUILD-SPECIFIC; `lean-hw` has its own).
* `Ct/Sha256.lean`   the rest of `sha256.rs`.
* `Ct/Heads.lean`    the heads (first 16 bytes) of the blocks of `chain_blocks`, `HeadsEq`.
* `Ct/Hash.lean`     constant-time lemmas for `hash.rs` (and `xmss::hash2`), except:
* `Ct/ChainTop.lean` `hash::chain_blocks` (BUILD-SPECIFIC; `lean-hw` has its own).
* `Ct/Wots.lean`     `util.rs`, `wots.rs`.
* `Ct/Xmss.lean`     `xmss.rs` (`xmss_node` by strong induction on the height).
* `Ct/Fors.lean`     `fors.rs` (including the new `fors_pk_gen`).
* `Ct/Slh.lean`      key generation, `api.public_key`, digest helpers, one `ht_sign` layer,
                     verification (`Rel.refl`).
* `Ct/Sim.lean`      one-sided simulation: `Rel.sim`, `loop_sim`, `loop_post`, inversion lemmas.
* `Ct/SignFacts.lean` functional facts used by signing (from `Slhdsa/Proofs` via erasure).
* `Ct/Sign.lean`     the signing simulators `slhdsa_leak.Sim.*` and the simulation theorems.
* `Ct/Theorems.lean` the headline theorems (K), (S), (V) with `#print axioms`.
* `Ct/Encoding.lean` `encoding.rs`: key comparison, raw keys, PKCS#8 and SPKI (with its
                     headline statements and `#print axioms`).
-/
